  - multi-user
  - household
  - privacy
  - clarifying questions
  - LLM evaluation
abstract: >-
  Two test suites for language-model agents that act for one member of a shared household.
  clarify: 48 decision environments in which an agent may buy one noisy clarifying question before
  delivering a personalised offer on a shared account, scored by regret against the exact optimum.
  dispute: 960 threads in which two members give opposite instructions about a memory entry that
  describes both, scored by whose instruction the agent carries out (last-speaker and account-holder effects).
